// A type-associated `comptime` constant is read as `V::N` (SPEC: "a type comptime is read as Type::NAME").
// `.` on the type is the constructor spelling; a READ through it is rejected naming the `::` form. The
// call form (`V.tag()`) has been refused for a long time (xfail/dot_on_type_static); the read form used to
// emit `(V).N` and reach the C compiler.
type value V {
    public comptime int32 N = 4;
    public ctor make() { }
}
fn int32 main() { return V.N; }   // ERROR: read it as `V::N`
